  "description": "A conflict story (paint against stain) is reviewed twice with no_change, and the first review is withdrawn on Wednesday. The other review remains in effect, so the story stays reviewed, and A-601's Thursday brown-paint does not continue it: maintenance records a related story whose detection relates to it, and the open-stories read lists the related story with the reviewed one superseded. When the second review is withdrawn too, the story reads unreviewed, and A-601's Saturday grey-paint continues the family's latest story, the related one, with a second detection.",
  "note": "7.3.1 *Withdrawn reviews*: \"After a review is withdrawn, and no other review of the story remains in effect at the withdrawal's effective time (6.7.9), 7.2.5 governs changes from that time. They continue the family's latest story, and an earlier story stays as recorded. While another review of the story remains in effect, changed evidence still opens a related story as above.\" 6.7.9: \"Withdrawing a review returns the story to `unreviewed` from the withdrawal's effective time, unless another review of the story remains in effect at that time (9.5.2).\"",
